  "objective": "CLOSE THE ALBANESE LEG. Roadmap AJC.albanese and its three children (.codim1, .symmetric, .universal). The headline universal-property theorem is ALREADY sorry-free \u2014 what is missing is the construction layer beneath it, so this task is about supplying real inputs to a statement that already stands, not about restating anything.\n\nTHREE FRONTS, with the actual sorry sites.\n\n (a) CODIMENSION-ONE RATIONAL-MAP EXTENSION (AJC.albanese.codim1). Albanese/CodimOneExtension.lean: CodimOneFree (:216, :218), gammaSpecField_ringEquiv (:752), localRing_dvr_of_codim_one (:1402), indeterminacy_pure_codim_one_into_grpScheme (:1751). Finish the diagonal-intersection and function-field pullback steps showing a rational map to an abelian variety has no codimension-one indeterminacy. The blueprint frontier flags Milne Lemma 3.3 (pure-codim-1 structure of the indeterminacy locus into a group variety) as 22 unlocks / 23 uses \u2014 the highest-leverage node in this cone, and the sibling Rebuild has a whole Albanese/CodimOne* family (CodimOneMilne31, CodimOneStalkRegularity, CodimOneDVRStalk, CodimOneSmoothReduced) covering the same ground. READ THOSE FIRST.\n\n (b) ABEL-JACOBI AND SYMMETRIC POWERS (AJC.albanese.symmetric). Albanese/AlbaneseUP.lean: abelJacobi (:335), SymmetricPower (:382), symmetricPowerAVMap (:416), symmetricPowerToJacobian (:453), descentThroughBirationalSigma (:496), albanese_eq_iff_symmetricPower_eq (:533). Six honest construction and bridge gaps: Abel-Jacobi, the symmetric-power carrier and quotient API, symmetric sums, the map to Pic0, birational descent, the factorisation connector. The characteristic-free symmetric-power route is already specified cleanly in the blueprint \u2014 follow it rather than inventing a route.\n\n (c) THE UNIVERSAL PROPERTY (AJC.albanese.universal). Complete descent through the birational g-th symmetric power and the factorisation biconditional. The connector now has the correct two directions: pointed rigidity plus quotient uniqueness forward, restriction along Q -> Q+(g-1)P0 backward. Two typed-sorry bridges; once they close, the existing theorem stands unconditionally.\n\nRIGIDITY IS YOURS TOO, if it blocks you: RigidityLemma.lean has three open obligations (:481 saturated-open-to-affine, :673 dense-open, :764 rigidity_core) and pointed rigidity is a direct input to (c).\n\nDISCIPLINE. Search before proving \u2014 horizon search spans your project, the sibling Rebuild, the standalone SubProjects/Albanese, and mathlib. The Rebuild Albanese/ directory is 24 files / 7.3k lines and its codim-one family is more developed than yours in places. Use the LSP loop between edits, lake build at session boundaries.\n\nCOORDINATION. You are one of four AJC teams. You consume Pic0 facts from ajc-pic0av (degree map, Pic0(k) = ker degree) \u2014 ask on the AJC conversation thread rather than proving them yourself or editing Picard/. Your files are Albanese/ and RigidityLemma.lean. Never edit files outside Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge.",
